{
  "version": 1,
  "_doc": "Mission briefings and the discovery rules (GDD sections 6, 7 and 15), read by src/tycoon/project/briefing_desk.gd, mission_fit.gd and discovery.gd. A briefing tells a situation in story form (TY_BF_<ID>_TITLE / _STORY / _GOAL in i18n/tycoon_project_strings.csv) and never says how to solve it. Its hidden 'solution' scores the player's choices: targets / types (1.0 = what the client hoped for, lower = it still helps, missing = it does not answer the question), 'need' (module ids the job cannot do without) and an optional 'ratio' (the client's own ideal balance of eng / sci / ops / rel, instead of the mission type's). A briefing appears on the board from its era once the agency can fly its best type and target and build its needed modules. reward = reward_base * size(best type) * era_mult[era] * reward_mult; budget = budget_mult * the estimate of the best plan; deadline in weeks after accepting. kinds: science (a research question), contract (a client: 'client' is a sponsor name key of contracts.json), space_apps (a NASA Space Apps style challenge), dream (a Cometling of the staff dreams it), race (a milestone of the race). 'card' links the encyclopedia card whose fact the story uses; 'teaches' {env: [targets]} reveals a target's hidden environment once the briefing is taken (its story tells it). 'voices' [{legend, key}]: the Lendas tied to the mission; the first one around (an arrived mentor or a hired Lenda) narrates it on the card, before the hints (TycoonLegends.briefing_voice; TY_BF_<ID>_VOICE). 'dreamer': the Lenda whose dream it is (kind dream). solution.antenna: the antennas that answer the client (any one), instead of the type's needs_antenna. Missions and client texts follow docs: Cometworks - Catalogo Completo de Missoes v2 (ratios for every catalogued mission).",
